Package: virtbase-pve-patches
Architecture: all
Depends: libpve-storage-perl,
         patch,
         qemu-server,
         ${misc:Depends},
Description: Proxmox VE patches for managing guest hookscripts via the API
 Three changes to Proxmox VE that are not upstream:
  * the storage upload API accepts the snippets content type,
  * an uploaded snippet that starts with "#!" is made executable, so it can
    serve as a guest hookscript,
  * users with VM.Config.Options may set a guest's hookscript, which upstream
    reserves for root@pam.
 .
 A hookscript runs as root on the node. With these patches, a user who may
 upload snippets and edit a guest's options can run code as root on the node.
 .
 libpve-storage-perl and qemu-server own the patched files, so upgrading either
 reverts the patches. A dpkg file trigger reapplies them whenever a package
 writes to /usr/share/perl5/PVE, and a daily systemd timer catches changes made
 outside dpkg. The patch state is published for the Prometheus node_exporter
 textfile collector.
